{# What the services report about this deployment (RC-28).

   The same contribution the health check reads (UIEvent.DEPLOYMENT_STATE), only
   rendered instead of judged: sleep-mode says a deployment sleeps, and without this a
   user sees a deployment with nothing running and no explanation why. Generic on
   purpose -- it loops over whatever facts the services report, so a second service that
   parks a deployment in a situation gets this block for free and no service name
   appears here.

   Since RC-35 the card carries a badge from the same facts, so what goes where is fixed:
   the BADGE names the situation in one or two words ("Slaapstand", "Uitgeschakeld"), this
   BLOCK carries the sentence that does not fit on a badge -- why it is so, and what makes
   it end. A fact therefore writes its ``summary`` for this block and its ``badge`` for the
   card; neither is a shortened version of the other. #}
{% set deployment_state_facts = deployment_state_facts | default({}) %}
{% for deployment in project.deployments | sort(attribute='name') %}
{% set facts = deployment_state_facts.get(deployment.name, []) %}
{% if facts %}
<div class="deployment-section" data-deployment="{{ deployment.name }}"
     {% if not loop.first %}class="is-hidden"{% endif %}>
    <c-layout-flow gap="md">
        {% for fact in facts %}
        <c-card outline="true" padding="lg" backgroundColor="grijs-050">
            <c-layout-row gap="md" verticalSpacing="center">
                <c-icon icon="info" size="lg" color="grijs-500" />
                <div>
                    <strong>{{ ServiceAdapter.get_service_definition(ServiceAdapter.get_service_by_value(fact.service)).name }}</strong>
                    <p class="rvo-text--sm rvo-text--subtle">{{ fact.summary }}</p>
                </div>
            </c-layout-row>
        </c-card>
        {% endfor %}
    </c-layout-flow>
</div>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
